      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Stripe errors can be frustrating, but let's break it down. You're experiencing a 402 error, which is a \"Payment Method Not Found\" error. It's likely that Stripe is unable to find the payment method in your test environment. \n\nYou can start by checking your test card information in the Stripe dashboard. Make sure the card number, expiration date, and CVV are correct. It's also possible that the card is being flagged as a test card, which might not be accepted by Stripe's servers. \n\nTo debug this, you can try adding the `test` parameter to your Stripe API request. This will tell Stripe that the card is a test card, and it might help resolve the issue. However, be aware that test cards can be revoked at any time, so this might not always work.\n\nAnother possibility is that the card is being flagged as a \"test\" card due to the CVV being invalid. You can try updating the CVV to a valid one or using a different test card.\n\nIt's also worth noting that Stripe has a \"test\" card limit, so if you're using a large number of test cards, you might be hitting this limit. You can try using a different test card or updating",
